      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the docs (page 126), \n\n\u003e UMA operation can be disabled by setting `UMA_LOCK` bit in `UMA_ECTS` register to 1. Once set to 1 it cannot be cleared by the firmware; only a Core Domain reset.\n\nIf RO sets `UMA_LOCK` bit in `UMA_ECTS` to 1 (calls `flash_uma_lock(1)`), and then in RW we call `crec_flash_pre_init()`, we\u0027ll try to call `flash_uma_lock(0)`.\n\nThat will [set `all_protected` to `0`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/flash.c;l\u003d314;drc\u003d1a77532e380bf2432a327cafa8b30220db8cbbe6), but [`\tUPDATE_BIT(NPCX_UMA_ECTS...)`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/flash.c;l\u003d315;drc\u003d1a77532e380bf2432a327cafa8b30220db8cbbe6) won\u0027t have any effect, right? And then `all_protected` is out of sync with `NPCX_UMA_ECTS`.\n\nDoes that mean we should change `flash_uma_lock` to be a no-op if `enable` is false?:\n\n```\nstatic void flash_uma_lock(int enable)\n{\n        if (!enable) return;\n        \n\tif (enable \u0026\u0026 !all_protected) {\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * Store SR1 / SR2 for later use since we\u0027re about to lock\n\t\t * out all access (including read access) to these regs.\n\t\t */\n\t\tflash_get_status(\u0026saved_sr1, \u0026saved_sr2);\n\t}\n\n\tall_protected \u003d enable;\n\tUPDATE_BIT(NPCX_UMA_ECTS, NPCX_UMA_ECTS_UMA_LOCK, enable);\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "9d089be335a3a3cb9b7470c424d790a6940f2685",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
